# Visual-capture artifacts are EPHEMERAL — never tracked. The harness writes
# capture PNGs + composites + manifests/logs into a caller-chosen output dir
# (demo/, shell-demo/, peasant/, shell/, smoke/, sxs/, sxs-smoke/, sxs-shell/, MANIFEST*, *.log);
# defaults land in /tmp, but if a run points its output dir inside this folder these patterns keep
# them out of git. sxs-smoke/ (smoke-surface SxS) and sxs-shell/ (shell/nav-surface SxS) are kept
# as DISTINCT subdirs from the legacy sxs/ (transcript/changes) so reviewers never confuse smoke
# evidence for shell evidence (see stitch-sxs.mjs SXS_OUT_SUBDIR).
#
# Allowlist: only the tracked harness scripts + docs live here. Add a new
# `!path` line to track any future script.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!probe-peasant.mjs
!selection-recovery-probe.mjs
!peasant-shoot.mjs
!boot-peasant.mjs
!shell-nav-gate.mjs
!shell-nav-default-gate.mjs
!surface-gate.mjs
!stitch-sxs.mjs
!changes-shoot.mjs
!demo-shoot.mjs
!full-app-smoke.mjs
!smoke-surfaces.mjs
!png-diff.mjs
!determinism.mjs
!transcript-input-gate.mjs
!validate-mock-coordinates.mjs
!strike-smoke-fixture.mjs
!search-share-visual.mjs
!testdata/
!testdata/transcript-input.yaml
!testdata/search-share.yaml
# baseline/ holds the committed golden references (not ephemeral captures) so the
# gates are self-contained — no /tmp dependency.
!baseline/
!baseline/**
# Retired baselines are dead artifacts and must not be re-added: the shell
# baseline, and the pre-composite-migration sibling-package golden.
baseline/shell-baseline/
baseline/tb/
# Generated smoke captures and SxS composites are local review artifacts. Keep them
# ignored so visual runs do not dirty the repository; record durable evidence in Beads.
